    "result_text": "Green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI agree with the finding \u2014 the July-cutoff fiscal-year rule was encoded twice (inline in `ClinicServiceImpl.generateMemberId` and as `OwnerMapper.fiscalYearEndYear`), inviting exactly the drift the reviewer flagged.\n\n**Fix \u2014 one home for the rule:**\n- Added `public static int BusinessDays.fiscalYearEndYear(LocalDate)` encoding the July-cutoff naming rule, placed alongside `effectiveRegistrationDate` since that class already owns registration-date policy. Its Javadoc states explicitly that *which* date to feed it (e.g. the business-day-adjusted registration date) is a separate decision left to the caller \u2014 making the business-day-adjustment question a single deliberate choice rather than accidental drift.\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.generateMemberId` now calls `BusinessDays.fiscalYearEndYear(...)` (fed the effective registration date, as before).\n- `OwnerMapper` deleted its local `fiscalYearEndYear` and routes both call sites (`formatMembershipPoints` tenure calc and the `formatFiscalYear` fallback) to `BusinessDays.fiscalYearEndYear`.\n\nOn the write/read date difference: with the rule now centralized, the remaining distinction is purely *which date* each caller supplies. The write path adjusts because `registrationDate` may be unset at generation time; the mapper reads the already-persisted (adjusted) date or parses the `FY` segment straight out of the `memberId`, so in practice they agree. I left the mapper fallback feeding `owner.getRegistrationDate()` directly (unchanged behaviour, including returning `null` when absent) and documented the date-choice as the caller's responsibility.\n\n**Minor/optional note on segment layout:** I left the write-constructs / read-parses split as-is. The parse side is already consolidated in the one private `memberIdRegion` helper (reused by both `formatLocality` and `formatFiscalYear`), so the \"2 digits after the region\" offset lives in a single place on the read side; a fuller shared layout descriptor felt like more indirection than this small, localized split warrants.\n\nAcceptance behaviour intact: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
